title: EMS Distro Architecture

files:
  - em.prog:em.examples.basic/Ex02_BlinkerP.em.ts
  - .assets/img-103-01-02.png
  - .assets/img-103-01-03.png

steps:
  - cmds:
      - open 1
    text: |
      {[ht,$start]Welcome}

      {[tr,101/01/01]}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * portable EMS programs so far
      * distro package supplies target support
      * orientation and vocabulary only

  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,$look]EMS Distro Architecture}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * board and setup status
      * portable program packages
      * selected distro package
      * generated build output
      * steady-state architecture

  - cmds:
      - view 3
    text: |
      {[ht,$look]Inside a Distro Package}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * rpi.2040 as the working example
      * distro bucket
      * MCU bucket
      * gist bucket
      * setup choices
      * name landmarks without opening sources

  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]Selecting a Board}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * board identifies target hardware
      * board implies a distro package
      * point to the board status item
      * callback to earlier BoardC exposure

  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]Selecting a Setup}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * setup is a build option for the board
      * board narrows available setup choices
      * point to the setup status item
      * examples: default, flash, sram

  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]From Sources to a Build}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * BoardC binds portable services to target implementations
      * BuildC drives generated build output
      * name both bridges without opening either source
      * keep generated artifacts at map level

  - cmds:
      - open 1
    text: |
      {[ht,$extra]Extra Credit}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * select another board
      * select another setup
      * rebuild a familiar portable program
      * observe status and output changes
      * no hardware or execution required

  - cmds:
      - open 1
    text: |
      {[ht,$steps]Next Steps}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * Tour 1 showed the normal steady-state architecture
      * Tour 2 introduces bare-metal bring-up
      * minimal BuildC
      * Gist01
      * direct $R access
      * generated artifacts and Wokwi execution
